# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .env.free_bots.example — Environment Variables Template for Free Bots
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# INSTRUCTIONS
# ────────────
# 1. Copy this file to .env  (it may already exist from the premium bot setup)
# 2. Fill in each BOT_N_TOKEN with the token from @BotFather
# 3. Set ADMIN_USER_ID to your own Telegram user ID
# 4. Leave any unused bot tokens blank — the runner will skip them gracefully
#
# SECURITY
# ────────
# • Never commit .env to git.  Add it to .gitignore immediately.
# • These are LIVE tokens — treat them like passwords.
#
# HOW TO GET A TOKEN
# ──────────────────
# 1. Open Telegram and search for @BotFather
# 2. Send /newbot  and follow the prompts
# 3. Copy the token BotFather gives you
#
# HOW TO GET YOUR USER ID
# ───────────────────────
# Send /start to @userinfobot on Telegram — it replies with your numeric ID
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Free Bot Tokens ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Match these with token_env values in free_bots_config.yaml
BOT_1_TOKEN=8667335611:AAEgL3I5HKFdE2vnIN2FGO4v-gxhSkROYCc
BOT_2_TOKEN=8776534031:AAHRjCBm1pNA7sbP-xbS_PGy8YMHbntpbdw
BOT_3_TOKEN=
BOT_4_TOKEN=
BOT_5_TOKEN=
BOT_6_TOKEN=
BOT_7_TOKEN=
BOT_8_TOKEN=
BOT_9_TOKEN=

# ── Admin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your Telegram numeric user ID — gives access to /stats and /broadcast
ADMIN_USER_ID=7708376300

# ── Shared Free-User Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the SQLite file shared by all free bots
# Relative paths are resolved from the directory where free_bot_runner.py runs
FREE_USERS_DB=free_users.db
